From da3f8c1e5b391300b77242c10f40d6382ddc00e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:28:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] RISC OS: a centred playground with black borders

In full screen (borderless) the Resolution in System Options is the size
of the playground. When it is smaller than the screen, the logical size
comes from it (getPlaygroundResolution), SDL_RenderSetIntegerScale centres
it at the largest whole-number scale that fits and maps the mouse to
match, and the presenter draws it there with black borders. The screen's
own size fills the screen as before. video.centred records the choice;
switching to borderless full screen clears it.
---
